  "grammar": [
    {
      "id": "u02_l1_g1",
      "pattern": "V-아/어 보다",
      "meaning_uz": "-ib ko'rmoq: biror narsani sinab ko'rish yoki tajriba qilish",
      "meaning_en": "Try doing: to do something to see what it's like, or to have the experience",
      "explanation_md": "**-아/어 보다** fe'lga qo'shilib, o'zbekchadagi **\"-ib ko'rmoq\"** ma'nosini beradi: *kiyib ko'rmoq, yeb ko'rmoq, borib ko'rmoq*.\n\n### Qanday yasaladi\n\n1. Fe'lning lug'at shaklidan **-다** olib tashlanadi: 입다 → **입**\n2. O'zakning oxirgi unlisiga qarab **-아** yoki **-어** qo'shiladi (xuddi **-아요/어요** dagi kabi): 입 + 어 → **입어**\n3. Keyin **보다** qo'shiladi va u tuslanadi: 입어 **보세요**, 입어 **봤어요**\n\n### Eng ko'p ishlatiladigan shakllar\n\n- **-아/어 보세요** — *\"...-ib ko'ring\"*. Do'konda sotuvchi, maslahat berganda ko'p ishlatiladi: **한번 입어 보세요** — *Bir kiyib ko'ring.*\n- **-아/어 봤어요** — *\"...-ib ko'rganman\"*, tajriba haqida: **김치를 먹어 봤어요** — *Kimchini yeb ko'rganman.*\n- Savol: **제주도에 가 봤어요?** — *Chejudoga borib ko'rganmisiz?*\n\n### Esda tuting\n\n- **한번** (\"bir\") so'zi ko'pincha shu qolip bilan birga keladi va iltimosni yumshatadi.\n- Tajriba haqida gapirganda o'tgan zamon **-아/어 봤어요** ishlatiladi. Oddiy **갔어요** — *\"bordim\"* (bir marta, aniq voqea), **가 봤어요** — *\"borib ko'rganman\"* (hayotimda shunday tajriba bo'lgan).\n- **보다** fe'lining o'zi bilan bu qolip ishlatilmaydi: \"봐 보세요\" o'rniga shunchaki **보세요** deyiladi.",
      "explanation_md_en": "**-아/어 보다** is added to a verb and means **\"try doing\"**: *try on, try eating, try going*.\n\n### How to form it\n\n1. Drop **-다** from the dictionary form: 입다 → **입**\n2. Add **-아** or **-어** depending on the last vowel of the stem (just like in **-아요/어요**): 입 + 어 → **입어**\n3. Then add **보다** and conjugate it: 입어 **보세요**, 입어 **봤어요**\n\n### The most common forms\n\n- **-아/어 보세요** — *\"try (doing)…\"*. Shop staff use it a lot, and so does anyone giving advice: **한번 입어 보세요** — *Try it on.*\n- **-아/어 봤어요** — *\"I've tried / I have done…\"*, about experience: **김치를 먹어 봤어요** — *I've eaten kimchi.*\n- Question: **제주도에 가 봤어요?** — *Have you ever been to Jeju Island?*\n\n### Remember\n\n- The word **한번** (\"once\") often comes with this pattern and makes the request softer.\n- For experience, use the past **-아/어 봤어요**. Plain **갔어요** means *\"I went\"* (one specific event); **가 봤어요** means *\"I have been there\"* (I've had that experience).\n- This pattern is not used with **보다** itself: instead of \"봐 보세요\" just say **보세요**.",
      "formation": [
        {
          "condition_uz": "Oxirgi unli ㅏ yoki ㅗ",
          "condition_en": "Last vowel ㅏ or ㅗ",
          "rule": "-아 보다",
          "example": "가다 → 가 보다, 오다 → 와 보다"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "Boshqa unlilar",
          "condition_en": "Other vowels",
          "rule": "-어 보다",
          "example": "입다 → 입어 보다, 먹다 → 먹어 보다"
        },
        {
          "condition_uz": "하다 bilan tugasa",
          "condition_en": "Ends in 하다",
          "rule": "해 보다",
          "example": "운동하다 → 운동해 보다"
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "ko": "이 치마 한번 입어 보세요.",
          "uz": "Bu yubkani bir kiyib ko'ring.",
          "en": "Try this skirt on.",
          "audio": "ea3f975d1cf7.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "김치를 먹어 봤어요?",
          "uz": "Kimchini yeb ko'rganmisiz?",
          "en": "Have you ever eaten kimchi?",
          "audio": "4b714ae32daf.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "네, 먹어 봤어요. 맛있어요.",
          "uz": "Ha, yeb ko'rganman. Mazali.",
          "en": "Yes, I have. It's tasty.",
          "audio": "d1257c7c7a35.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "제주도에 가 봤어요.",
          "uz": "Chejudoga borib ko'rganman.",
          "en": "I've been to Jeju Island.",
          "audio": "5ceaaf7b8dc5.mp3"
        },
        {
          "ko": "한국 노래를 들어 보세요.",
          "uz": "Koreys qo'shiqlarini tinglab ko'ring.",
          "en": "Try listening to Korean songs.",
          "audio": "795daaf5c43f.mp3"
        }
      ],
      "mistakes": [
        {
          "wrong": "입 보세요",
          "right": "입어 보세요",
          "why_uz": "-아/어 qismi tushib qolgan: o'zakka avval -어 qo'shiladi, keyin 보다 keladi.",
          "why_en": "The -아/어 part is missing: first add -어 to the stem, then 보다."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "가어 보세요",
          "right": "가 보세요",
          "why_uz": "가다 ning unlisi ㅏ, shuning uchun -아 qo'shiladi va 가 + 아 = 가 bo'lib qisqaradi.",
          "why_en": "The vowel of 가다 is ㅏ, so -아 is added, and 가 + 아 shortens to 가."
        },
        {
          "wrong": "한국에 가 보요",
          "right": "한국에 가 봐요",
          "why_uz": "보다 ham oddiy fe'l kabi tuslanadi: 보 + 아요 = 봐요.",
          "why_en": "보다 conjugates like any other verb: 보 + 아요 = 봐요."
        }
      ],
      "uz_compare": "O'zbek tilida ham aynan shunday qurilma bor: fe'l + -ib + ko'rmoq. 입어 보다 = kiyib ko'rmoq, 먹어 보다 = yeb ko'rmoq. So'z tartibi ham bir xil: avval asosiy fe'l, keyin 'ko'rmoq'. Shuning uchun 입어 보세요 ni 'kiyib ko'ring' deb, 먹어 봤어요 ni 'yeb ko'rganman' deb eslab qoling.",
      "compare_en": "English has a close match: 'try + -ing'. 입어 보다 = try on, 먹어 보다 = try eating. For experience, English uses 'have you ever…?': 먹어 봤어요? = Have you ever eaten it? So remember 입어 보세요 as 'try it on' and 먹어 봤어요 as 'I've eaten it (before)'."
    },
    {
      "id": "u02_l1_g2",
      "pattern": "입다 · 신다 · 쓰다 · 끼다 · 차다 · 하다",
      "meaning_uz": "Kiyish fe'llari: nimani kiyishga qarab fe'l o'zgaradi",
      "meaning_en": "Verbs for wearing: the verb depends on what you put on",
      "explanation_md": "O'zbek tilida deyarli hamma narsani **\"kiymoq\"** deymiz. Koreys tilida esa fe'l narsa **tananing qaysi qismiga** kiyilishiga qarab tanlanadi.\n\n| Tana qismi | Fe'l | Misol |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tana (ust kiyim) | **입다** | 바지를 입어요 |\n| Oyoq | **신다** | 운동화를 신어요 |\n| Bosh, yuz | **쓰다** | 모자를 써요, 안경을 써요 |\n| Barmoq, qo'l | **끼다** | 반지를 껴요, 장갑을 껴요 |\n| Bilak, bel | **차다** | 시계를 차요 |\n| Aksessuar | **하다** | 목도리를 해요 |\n\n### Tuslanishga e'tibor bering\n\n- **쓰다** → **써요** (ㅡ tushib qoladi), o'tgan zamon **썼어요**\n- **끼다** → **껴요** (ㅣ + 어 = ㅕ), o'tgan zamon **꼈어요**\n- **차다** → **차요**, o'tgan zamon **찼어요**\n\n### Yechmoq\n\nKo'pchilik narsa uchun **벗다** ishlatiladi: 옷을 벗어요, 신발을 벗어요, 모자를 벗어요. Uzukni **빼다** (반지를 빼요), soatni **풀다** (시계를 풀어요) bilan yechamiz.\n\nKoreyada uyga kirganda **신발을 벗어요** — poyabzal yechiladi!",
      "explanation_md_en": "In English we use **\"wear\"** or **\"put on\"** for almost everything. In Korean the verb depends on **which part of the body** the item goes on.\n\n| Body part | Verb | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| Body (clothes) | **입다** | 바지를 입어요 |\n| Feet | **신다** | 운동화를 신어요 |\n| Head, face | **쓰다** | 모자를 써요, 안경을 써요 |\n| Fingers, hands | **끼다** | 반지를 껴요, 장갑을 껴요 |\n| Wrist, waist | **차다** | 시계를 차요 |\n| Accessories | **하다** | 목도리를 해요 |\n\n### Watch the conjugation\n\n- **쓰다** → **써요** (ㅡ drops), past **썼어요**\n- **끼다** → **껴요** (ㅣ + 어 = ㅕ), past **꼈어요**\n- **차다** → **차요**, past **찼어요**\n\n### Taking things off\n\nFor most things use **벗다**: 옷을 벗어요, 신발을 벗어요, 모자를 벗어요. A ring is taken off with **빼다** (반지를 빼요), a watch with **풀다** (시계를 풀어요).\n\nIn Korea you **take your shoes off** (**신발을 벗어요**) when you enter a home!",
